ICML-2023-P0091,ICML-2023-A000395,Junfei Xia,stacked,2,2,8,"vergences in the current vector field. Reconstructing ocean currents accurately can facilitate weather forecasting, maritime navigation, and forecasting of oil spill dispersion. And current divergences are important to identify since they are responsible for the transport of biomass, carbon, and nutrients – with implications for ecosystem management, climate, and the fishing industry (D’Asaro et al., ). With these tasks in mind, researchers release and track GPS-tagged buoys in the ocean (Özgökmen, ; D’Asaro et al., ).",-2,data/raw/icml/2023/first_pages/ICML-2023-P0091.txt,https://proceedings.mlr.press/v202/berlinghieri23a/berlinghieri23a.pdf
