ICML-2023-P0181,ICML-2023-A000794,Liping Liu,numbered,0,3,4,UNKNOWN,-1000,data/raw/icml/2023/first_pages/ICML-2023-P0181.txt,https://proceedings.mlr.press/v202/chen23k/chen23k.pdf
ICML-2023-P0181,ICML-2023-A000791,Xiaohui Chen,stacked,2,3,4,"There are only a few deep generative models designed for generating large graphs: NetGAN (Bojchevski et al., ) and CELL (Rendsburg et al., ) are two examples. However, recent research (Chanpuriya et al., ) shows that these two models are edge-independent models and have a theoretical limitation: they cannot reproduce several important statistics (e.g. triangle counts and clustering coefficient) in their generated graphs unless they memorize the training graph. A list of other models (Chanpuriya et al., ) including Variational Graph Autoencoders (VGAE) (Kipf & Welling, 2016b) and GraphVAE (Simonovsky & Komodakis, ) are also edge-independent models and share the same limitation.",-2,data/raw/icml/2023/first_pages/ICML-2023-P0181.txt,https://proceedings.mlr.press/v202/chen23k/chen23k.pdf
ICML-2023-P0181,ICML-2023-A000792,Jiaxing He,stacked,2,3,4,"There are only a few deep generative models designed for generating large graphs: NetGAN (Bojchevski et al., ) and CELL (Rendsburg et al., ) are two examples. However, recent research (Chanpuriya et al., ) shows that these two models are edge-independent models and have a theoretical limitation: they cannot reproduce several important statistics (e.g. triangle counts and clustering coefficient) in their generated graphs unless they memorize the training graph. A list of other models (Chanpuriya et al., ) including Variational Graph Autoencoders (VGAE) (Kipf & Welling, 2016b) and GraphVAE (Simonovsky & Komodakis, ) are also edge-independent models and share the same limitation.",-2,data/raw/icml/2023/first_pages/ICML-2023-P0181.txt,https://proceedings.mlr.press/v202/chen23k/chen23k.pdf
