ICML-2023-P0523,ICML-2023-A002291,Florian Heinrichs,stacked,2,3,3,"signal with one classification per window. The advantage of this approach is that only the most recent data is used for predictions, but it comes at cost: the signal of interest might occur at any time point in the extracted window. Thus, any classifier of the sliding windows needs to be “shift invariant” in the sense that it detects the desired signal independently of its position in the window.",-6,data/raw/icml/2023/first_pages/ICML-2023-P0523.txt,https://proceedings.mlr.press/v202/heinrichs23a/heinrichs23a.pdf
