ICML-2023-P0640,ICML-2023-A002823,Hiroshi Takahashi,stacked,2,3,6,"Various methods have been presented to search the adversarial examples, and Auto-Attack (Croce & Hein, ) is one of the most successful methods at finding the worst-case attacks. For trustworthy deep learning applications, classifiers should be robust against the worst-case attacks. To improve the robustness, many defense methods have also been presented (Kurakin et al., ; Madry et al., ; Wang et al., 2020b; Cohen et al., ). Among them, adversarial training is a promising method, which empirically achieves good robustness (Carmon et al., ; Kurakin et al., ; Madry et al., ). However, adversarial training is more difficult than standard training, e.g., it requires higher sample complexity (Schmidt et al., ; Wang et al., 2020a) and model capacity (Zhang et al., 2021b).",-6,data/raw/icml/2023/first_pages/ICML-2023-P0640.txt,https://proceedings.mlr.press/v202/kanai23a/kanai23a.pdf
ICML-2023-P0640,ICML-2023-A002824,Kentaro Ohno,stacked,2,3,6,"Various methods have been presented to search the adversarial examples, and Auto-Attack (Croce & Hein, ) is one of the most successful methods at finding the worst-case attacks. For trustworthy deep learning applications, classifiers should be robust against the worst-case attacks. To improve the robustness, many defense methods have also been presented (Kurakin et al., ; Madry et al., ; Wang et al., 2020b; Cohen et al., ). Among them, adversarial training is a promising method, which empirically achieves good robustness (Carmon et al., ; Kurakin et al., ; Madry et al., ). However, adversarial training is more difficult than standard training, e.g., it requires higher sample complexity (Schmidt et al., ; Wang et al., 2020a) and model capacity (Zhang et al., 2021b).",-6,data/raw/icml/2023/first_pages/ICML-2023-P0640.txt,https://proceedings.mlr.press/v202/kanai23a/kanai23a.pdf
ICML-2023-P0640,ICML-2023-A002825,Yasutoshi Ida,stacked,2,3,6,"Various methods have been presented to search the adversarial examples, and Auto-Attack (Croce & Hein, ) is one of the most successful methods at finding the worst-case attacks. For trustworthy deep learning applications, classifiers should be robust against the worst-case attacks. To improve the robustness, many defense methods have also been presented (Kurakin et al., ; Madry et al., ; Wang et al., 2020b; Cohen et al., ). Among them, adversarial training is a promising method, which empirically achieves good robustness (Carmon et al., ; Kurakin et al., ; Madry et al., ). However, adversarial training is more difficult than standard training, e.g., it requires higher sample complexity (Schmidt et al., ; Wang et al., 2020a) and model capacity (Zhang et al., 2021b).",-6,data/raw/icml/2023/first_pages/ICML-2023-P0640.txt,https://proceedings.mlr.press/v202/kanai23a/kanai23a.pdf
