ICML-2023-P0663,ICML-2023-A002916,Hamza Keurti,stacked,2,3,5,"Bernhard Schölkopf actions. Humans acquire such internal models by interacting with the world, but the learning principles allowing it remain elusive. We investigate how Machine Learning (ML) can shed light on this question, as it moves towards representations that carry more than just observational information (Sutton & Barto, ; Schölkopf et al., ) and develops tools for interactive and geometric structure learning (Cohen & Welling, ; Eslami et al., )",-4,data/raw/icml/2023/first_pages/ICML-2023-P0663.txt,https://proceedings.mlr.press/v202/keurti23a/keurti23a.pdf
