ICML-2023-P0724,ICML-2023-A003176,Stephan Günnemann,numbered,0,3,4,UNKNOWN,-1000,data/raw/icml/2023/first_pages/ICML-2023-P0724.txt,https://proceedings.mlr.press/v202/kosmala23a/kosmala23a.pdf
ICML-2023-P0724,ICML-2023-A003173,Arthur Kosmala,stacked,2,3,4,"despite recent success in understanding theoretically universal models (Gasteiger et al., ; Dym & Maron, ), computational constraints still hamper GNNs in learning long-ranged physical interactions between atoms: the standard notion of a molecular graph (if no hand-crafted bond information is used) treats atoms as vertices and connects them by an edge if their 3D distance is within a cutoff hyperparameter (Schütt et al., ). This can be a problem if more remote atom interactions contribute to a target: they are long-ranged also on the graph, potentially relating vertices many edges apart. There is ample empirical and theoretical evidence of limited GNN performance in this case, e.g., due to over-squashing (Alon & Yahav, ).",-10,data/raw/icml/2023/first_pages/ICML-2023-P0724.txt,https://proceedings.mlr.press/v202/kosmala23a/kosmala23a.pdf
