ICML-2023-P0810,ICML-2023-A003539,Arno Solin,symbol,1,0,3,UNKNOWN,-1000,data/raw/icml/2023/first_pages/ICML-2023-P0810.txt,https://proceedings.mlr.press/v202/li23m/li23m.pdf
ICML-2023-P0810,ICML-2023-A003537,Rui Li,stacked,2,2,3,"− . − . MCMC VI ELBO Ours Training proxy for. . . . . . test performance on holdout data − . − . Predictive density log p(y∗ ; θ) Approximate inference in Gaussian process (GP) models with non-conjugate likelihoods gets entangled with the learning of the model hyperparameters. We improve hyperparameter learning in GP models and focus on the interplay between variational inference (VI) and the learning target. While VI’s lower bound to the marginal likelihood is a suitable objective for inferring the approximate posterior, we show that a direct approximation of the marginal likelihood as in Expectation Propagation (EP) is a better learning objective for hyperparameter optimization. We design a hybrid training procedure to bring the best of both worlds: it leverages conjugatecomputation VI for inference and uses an EP-like marginal likelihood approximation for hyperparameter learning. We compare VI, EP, Laplace approximation, and our proposed training procedure and empirically demonstrate the effectiveness of our proposal across a wide range of data sets. − . Marginal likelihood log p(y; θ)",-18,data/raw/icml/2023/first_pages/ICML-2023-P0810.txt,https://proceedings.mlr.press/v202/li23m/li23m.pdf
ICML-2023-P0810,ICML-2023-A003538,S. T. John,stacked,2,2,3,UNKNOWN,-1000,data/raw/icml/2023/first_pages/ICML-2023-P0810.txt,https://proceedings.mlr.press/v202/li23m/li23m.pdf
ICML-2023-P0810,ICML-2023-A003539,Arno Solin,stacked,2,2,3,"− . − . MCMC VI ELBO Ours Training proxy for. . . . . . test performance on holdout data − . − . Predictive density log p(y∗ ; θ) Approximate inference in Gaussian process (GP) models with non-conjugate likelihoods gets entangled with the learning of the model hyperparameters. We improve hyperparameter learning in GP models and focus on the interplay between variational inference (VI) and the learning target. While VI’s lower bound to the marginal likelihood is a suitable objective for inferring the approximate posterior, we show that a direct approximation of the marginal likelihood as in Expectation Propagation (EP) is a better learning objective for hyperparameter optimization. We design a hybrid training procedure to bring the best of both worlds: it leverages conjugatecomputation VI for inference and uses an EP-like marginal likelihood approximation for hyperparameter learning. We compare VI, EP, Laplace approximation, and our proposed training procedure and empirically demonstrate the effectiveness of our proposal across a wide range of data sets. − . Marginal likelihood log p(y; θ)",-18,data/raw/icml/2023/first_pages/ICML-2023-P0810.txt,https://proceedings.mlr.press/v202/li23m/li23m.pdf
