ICML-2023-P0891,ICML-2023-A003899,Weiming Liu,stacked,2,3,4,"in improving online performance. Take heads-up no-limit Texas hold’em as an example. A common approach is to first generate a blueprint strategy using Counterfactual Regret Minimization (CFR) algorithms (Zinkevich et al., ; Lanctot et al., ; Tammelin et al., ) and abstraction techniques (Gilpin & Sandholm, ; Gilpin et al., ). When playing online, subgame-solving techniques (Burch et al., ; Moravcik et al., ; Brown & Sandholm, ; Brown et al., ; Zhang & Sandholm, ) are used to refine the blueprint strategy, making it less exploitable and hopefully more profitable.",-6,data/raw/icml/2023/first_pages/ICML-2023-P0891.txt,https://proceedings.mlr.press/v202/liu23k/liu23k.pdf
