ICML-2023-P0972,ICML-2023-A004299,Baorui Ma,stacked,2,3,3,"(a) Noisy Points (b) Denoised Points (c) Surface Reconstruction Figure . We introduce to learn signed distance functions (SDFs) for single noisy point clouds. Our method does not require ground truth signed distances, point normals or clean points as supervision for training. We achieve this via learning a mapping from one noisy observation to another or even on a single observation. Our novel learning manner is supported by modern Lidar systems which capture to noisy observations per second. We show the SDF learned from (a) a single real scan containing 10M points, (b) the denoised point cloud and (c) the reconstructed surface. Fig. demonstrates our superiority over the latest surface reconstructions in this case.",-6,data/raw/icml/2023/first_pages/ICML-2023-P0972.txt,https://proceedings.mlr.press/v202/ma23d/ma23d.pdf
