ICML-2023-P1268,ICML-2023-A005530,Pierre-Alexandre Mattei,symbol,1,0,4,UNKNOWN,-1000,data/raw/icml/2023/first_pages/ICML-2023-P1268.txt,https://proceedings.mlr.press/v202/senetaire23a/senetaire23a.pdf
ICML-2023-P1268,ICML-2023-A005527,Hugo Henri Joseph Senetaire,stacked,2,4,4,"for black-box models, and we refer to Linardatos et al. ( ) for a recent survey. Finding interpretable models is hard. The lack of consensus for evaluating an explanation (Afchar et al., ; Jethani et al., 2021a; Liu et al., ; Hooker et al., ) makes it difficult to assess the qualities of the different methods. Many leads are explored such as interpretability for unsupervised models (Crabbé & van der Schaar, ; Moshkovitz et al., ), using concept embedding models to obtain high-level explanation (Zarlenga et al., ), global feature selection (Tibshirani, ; Lemhadri et al., ). In this paper, we will focus on methods that offer an understanding of which features are important for the prediction of a given instance in a supervised learning setting. These types of methods are called instance-wise feature selection and quantify how much a prediction changes when only a subset of features is shown to the model.",-6,data/raw/icml/2023/first_pages/ICML-2023-P1268.txt,https://proceedings.mlr.press/v202/senetaire23a/senetaire23a.pdf
