ICML-2023-P1659,ICML-2023-A007343,Mike Lewis,stacked,2,2,9,"(a) Overview of Retrieval-Augmented Multimodal Model (b) Dense Multimodal Retriever f(query, memory) → score Labrador sitting on bench near water. Generator (c) Retrieval-Augmented Generator (Multimodal Model) Loss for the retrieved docs score Mean Pooling Retriever Transformer Cosine similarity CLIP Text Encoder Mixed-modal Encoder Mixed-modal Encoder Query document Memory document (image or text or mixture) Loss for the main doc E.g. Extension of CLIP CLIP Image Encoder Retrieved Doc Labrador retriever Sitting on bench. Input document (image or text or mixture) Memory Retrieved Doc Labrador retriever sitting on bench. Labrador sitting on bench near water. Labrador retriever sitting by water. (Multimodal documents) Main Document Each image is mapped into tokens using VQGAN Figure . Our approach, retrieval-augmented multimodal modeling. (a) Overview: given an input multimodal document, we use a retriever to retrieve relevant multimodal documents from an external memory, and use the generator to refer to the retrieved documents and make predictions for the input (e.g., generate the continuation). (b) The multimodal retriever is a dense retriever with a mixed-modal encoder that can encode mixture of text and images ( . ). (c) The retrieval-augmented generator uses the CM3 Transformer architecture, and we prepend the retrieved documents to the main input document that we feed into the model ( . ). (a) Overview of Retrieval Augmented Multimodal Model",-4,data/raw/icml/2023/first_pages/ICML-2023-P1659.txt,https://proceedings.mlr.press/v202/yasunaga23a/yasunaga23a.pdf
