ICML-2023-P1733,ICML-2023-A007662,Haobo Zhang,stacked,2,4,4,"the estimator fˆ. One of the most popular non-parametric regression methods, the kernel method, aims to estimate fρ∗ using candidate functions from a reproducing kernel Hilbert space (RKHS) H, a separable Hilbert space associated to a kernel function k defined on X , e.g., Kohler & Krzyżak ( ); Cucker & Smale ( ); Caponnetto & de Vito ( ); Steinwart & Christmann ( ). This paper focuses on the kernel ridge regression (KRR), which constructs an estimator fˆλ by solving the penalized least square problem ! n 1X ˆ fλ = arg min (yi − f (xi )) + λ∥f ∥H , ( ) n i= f ∈H",-6,data/raw/icml/2023/first_pages/ICML-2023-P1733.txt,https://proceedings.mlr.press/v202/zhang23x/zhang23x.pdf
